Z||000022||stimpy||08-22-2001||10:48 PM||||I also have those front speakers and the same head unit. I have the front running through a Phase Linear (cheapie) 200w amp and they sound great. My rear speakers are running directly off the deck, and I can barely hear them. I also have the rear preamp outputs running to my amp for my BassShakers, so that may be a problem. But I think with more power you would be more impressed with the sound.<P>And maybe Alpine is "that good". ||||reg||1
Z||000023||fiero56||08-22-2001||11:39 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Jaei Sun:<BR><B>I hate Pioneer stuff it's pretty cheapy-- unless you get the high end.<P>Bostons all the way!</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Glad I'm not the only one Jaei Sun! I remember back when my stockers were going bad. After researching and never finding a 4x10 found worth my money/time, I ended up installing a set of Boston 6x9's in my dash, and have never looked back at 4x10 speakers. I've got some 4x6's picked out, just haven't bought and installed them yet.||||reg||1
